{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260523194126a7988ce2151b4778","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm the 快速原型师 (Rapid Prototyper) agent. I have one pending task:\n\n**Task ID 1**: 开发抖音小游戏消消消大作战，三消类match-3游戏。项目目录D:/games/match3-xiaoxiaoxiao/。用HTML5 Canvas，适配手机竖屏，符合抖音小游戏API，包含完整游戏循环和分数系统。完成后写入D:/loopcli/main/inbox/报告\n\nI need to:\n1. Develop a match-3 game called \"消消消大作战\" for Douyin (TikTok China) mini-game platform\n2. Use HTML5 Canvas\n3. Optimize for mobile portrait orientation\n4. Comply with Douyin mini-game API\n5. Include complete game loop and scoring system\n6. Project directory: D:/games/match3-xiaoxiaoxiao/\n\nLet me plan this out and start building. I need to create:\n1. The project structure at D:/games/match3-xiaoxiaoxiao/\n2. Game files with HTML5 Canvas\n3. Douyin mini-game compatible API\n4. Complete match-3 game mechanics\n5. Scoring system\n6. Mobile portrait optimization\n\nLet me start by creating the project directory and the game files. A typical Douyin mini-game uses a structure like:\n- game.js (or index.js) - main game entry\n- game.json - game configuration\n- project.config.json - project configuration\n\nActually, let me think about the Douyin mini-game API. Douyin mini-games (抖音小游戏) are based on a similar framework to WeChat mini-games but with some differences. The core API includes:\n- `tt.createCanvas()` - create canvas\n- `tt.createImage()` - create image\n- `tt.getSystemInfoSync()` - get system info\n- `tt.onTouchStart()`, `tt.onTouchMove()`, `tt.onTouchEnd()` - touch events\n- `tt.showModal()` - show modal\n- `tt.setStorageSync()` / `tt.getStorageSync()` - local storage\n\nLet me create a complete match-3 game with these features:\n- 8x8 grid of colorful gems/candies\n- Swap adjacent pieces to match 3 or more\n- Animations for matches and drops\n- Score system\n- Level system\n- Game over conditions\n- Mobile portrait layout\n- Touch controls\n\nLet me structure the project:\n\nD:/games/match3-xiaoxiaoxiao/\n├── game.js          - Main game entry point\n├── game.json        - Game configuration\n├── project.config.json - Project config\n├── js/\n│   ├── game.js      - Core game logic\n│   ├── board.js     - Board/grid management\n│   ├── renderer.js  - Canvas rendering\n│   ├── animations.js - Animation system\n│   ├── input.js     - Touch/input handling\n│   └── score.js     - Score management\n└── images/          - Game assets (if needed)\n\nActually, for a Douyin mini-game, the structure is simpler. Let me create a single-file approach that's clean and complete.\n\nFor Douyin mini-games, the basic structure is:\n- `game.js` - Entry point (like the main script)\n- `game.json` - Configuration\n- `project.config.json` - Project settings\n\nThe API prefix is `tt` (for 头条/TikTok).\n\nLet me create the complete game. I'll make it modular but in a single directory structure that's easy to understand.\n\nActually, I think the best approach for a prototype is to create a well-structured but manageable project. Let me create:\n\n1. `game.js` - Main entry point\n2. `game.json` - Configuration  \n3. `project.config.json` - Project config\n4. `js/engine.js` - Core game engine\n5. `js/renderer.js` - Rendering\n6. `js/input.js` - Input handling\n\nWait, for Douyin mini-games, the entry is `game.js` and it's more like a single-script environment. Let me look at what makes sense.\n\nActually, let me just create a clean, well-organized project. The Douyin mini-game platform uses CommonJS modules (require), so I can split into multiple files.\n\nLet me create the project structure:\n```\nD:/games/match3-xiaoxiaoxiao/\n├── game.js              # Entry point\n├── game.json            # Game config\n├── project.config.json  # Project config\n├── js/\n│   ├── board.js         # Board logic\n│   ├── renderer.js      # Canvas rendering\n│   ├── input.js         # Touch handling\n│   ├── animation.js     # Animations\n│   └── score.js       